## Session 72 summary

**Decisive progress: identified the true root of the `cache_coherency` / `unlink_visibility` blocker, confirmed by a GPT consult.**

### What I proved (RULE 4, all measured on clean-reboot runs)
- The unlink failure is **reader-staleness**: a peer-durably-deleted file stays visible on one node (1–3 survivors); all other nodes incl. the owner agree it's gone. In isolation there's no create-loss (the 16-file create-loss was a cumulative-run artifact).
- Traced the producer: dir EX/PR **fast-path re-grants** detect `stale_base` (`i_dlm_dir_gen > i_dlm_dir_loaded_gen`) but did no refresh.

### Acquire-side refresh is a DEAD END (4 variants, all reverted)
EX evict (unlink PASS / rename 0→40) → +`blkdev_issue_flush` barrier (rename 40→14) → +PR readers (rename PASS / unlink 3 survivors) → +conservative loaded_gen (unlink 24s→**500s** flush storm, still stale). Advancing `loaded_gen` serves stale forever; not advancing causes a flush storm. **The acquire side can't fix it because there's nothing newer on the medium to read.**

### THE REAL ROOT (GPT-confirmed) — write-side "publish before notify"
`mxfs_dlm_note_dir_modified` bumps peers' gen at commit but **never writes the modified dir block to the shared LUN**. Destage happens only via lazy xfsaild or the BAST-release fence — and in the 4-node all-cache-the-dir test **no node is ever BAST'd**, so deletes sit in each node's local cache forever. The durable variant `mxfs_dlm_dir_durable_signal` (log_force + bwrite + note) exists but **was never wired in**.

### Next session (design in `sess100_lessons`)
Wire in **publish-before-notify**: in `xfs_remove/create/rename`, post-commit (ILOCK held, outside txn) do `log_force(SYNC)` + `xfs_bwrite` modified dir blocks + `blkdev_issue_flush` + **then** bump gen; remove the in-txn `note_dir_modified` calls (xfs_dir2.c:411/633/696); treat rename as one visibility unit. Reader side then only needs gen-gated clear-DONE invalidate + plain re-read (no acquire-side flush). Start synchronous for correctness, then coalesce per-dir to manage the cost.

**Source reverted to ≈baseline (built `DB19A553`); deployed build on nodes is the regressed `84EA79C2` — next session builds the write-side fix and redeploys. Known-good baseline = `D6AD04FE` (3/4).**

